      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "At a craft store, a $12$-yard roll of copper wire costs $$19.80.$ What's the unit price per foot?\n\nAssume that there are $3$ feet in one yard.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert from yards to feet. There are $3$ feet in each yard, so we multiply the number of yards by $3:$  \n\n$$\n12\\times 3=36\n$$\n\nSo, $12$ yards is the same as $36$ feet. Now, to find the unit price per foot, we divide the total price by $36:$  \n\n$$\n19.80÷36=0.55\n$$\n\nTherefore, the copper wire costs $$0.55$ per foot.",
